  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 350°F (180°C) and line a sheet pan with parchment.",
    "Toss the diced sweet potato with the olive oil, oregano, salt and pepper. Spread in one layer and bake 25 min, until tender.",
    "Meanwhile, brown the beef in a large skillet over medium-high heat, breaking it up, 6 to 8 min, until no pink remains (160°F). Drain the fat, season with salt and pepper, stir in the black beans and cook 2 min to warm through.",
    "Make the salsa: stir together the red onion, tomatoes, cilantro, olive oil and salt.",
    "Divide the sweet potato, beef and beans among 4 bowls. Add the salsa and avocado.",
    "Top with more cilantro, the Parmesan and chili."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Most published sweet potato bowl recipes roast hotter, 425°F to 450°F for 18 to 23 min, for crisper edges. This one bakes at 350°F.",
    "Season the beef however you like. Taco seasoning works well here."
  ],
